Test vectors for Cocoon's Spaces primitives (space/), generated by running the
reference implementation as published for the October 22, 2026 alpha:

  packages: @atproto/space and @atproto/crypto 0.0.0-spaces-alpha-20261022141228
  source:   https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto
            branch permissioned-data-alpha, commit ac0c9f15392f6f0298d71dc52aa88c05036150be

gen-vectors.mjs (in this directory, with re-run instructions in its header)
writes all three files with fixed keys, after checking each vector with the
reference itself:

  vectors.json  set hashes, commit and record MACs and their headers, KEM
                encapsulations (key share and shared secret against a fixed
                #atproto_kem key), credential request signatures, and tokens
  export.star   a space repo as the reference's serializeRepo writes it for
                getRepo (STAR, atproto-space-repo profile), five records, one
                naming a blob
  export.json   that repo's commit, the shared secret and MAC header it was
                served with, and its records

Signatures, token jtis and KEM key shares are random, so a re-run changes only
those values (and the export's MAC header).

The HTTP signature, token, MAC, KEM and STAR test cases (space/*_test.go) are
ported from packages/space/src/{http-signature,star}.test.ts and
packages/space/tests/{credential,mac,kem,sync,repo-commit}.test.ts at the same
commit. kem_test.go also checks the RFC 9180 §A.3.1 DHKEM(P-256) vector.

